# Skill convenience scripts (.skills/**/*.sh) MUST be LF — on Windows
# git-bash, CRLF corrupts `set -euo pipefail` (the trailing \r is parsed
# as part of the option name, producing `set: pipefail : invalid option
# name` at exit 2). POSIX bash on Linux/macOS works either way, so the
# bug only fires for Windows local dev. Surfaced 2026-05-17 during the
# post-PR-242/243 wet validation.
.skills/**/*.sh text eol=lf
tests/skill-scripts/*.bats text eol=lf

# Canonical install / uninstall / build-artifact scripts + every bundled
# wrapper (scripts/**/*.sh) MUST be LF for the same reason as .skills/**/*.sh
# above: under Windows git-bash with core.autocrlf=true, CRLF corrupts
# `set -euo pipefail` (the trailing \r becomes part of the option name →
# `set: pipefail : invalid option name`, exit 2). Worse, scripts/build-artifact.sh
# `cp -r`s the wrappers into the release tarball, so a CRLF checkout would bake
# CRLF into every scripts/sh/run-*.sh and hard-fail on mac/Linux extraction.
# GH release builds (ubuntu-latest, core.autocrlf=false) were already safe; this
# closes the Windows-local-dev + cross-host-tarball corruption vector.
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/**/*.sh text eol=lf

